// Part 2 of judgement.PARTS of the typed family of test/fort/support/generator.ft under the
// closed-world judgement of test/fort/support/judgement.ft: the counts of the part, the count of
// its failures of each class of judgement.CLASSES, and two lines for each failure: the key of its
// function, then its class, its first error, its verdict and each other kind of error of its
// runs. Those lines are the list of the known failures of this part. A function that enters the
// list, one that leaves it and one that changes its class each change a line. The last line is
// the count that judgement.KNOWN lists for the part. The part must give the count of KNOWN for
// each class exactly: a failure with no class gives the exit status 1, and so does a count of a
// class that is above or below its row.
import judgement;

fn main(string@ args) i32 {
    return judgement.run_part(2, args);
}
